# TKT-1073, self-caught. .tira is intentionally excluded from here only in
# spirit, not by name: the Dockerfile's own `ADD .tira /test-project/.tira`
# line still needs it in the build context. The blanket `COPY .` destination
# (/root/.developer-dashboard/skills/tira) has it removed with a RUN step
# in the Dockerfile instead, right after that copy - see the comment there.
#
# .git is deliberately NOT excluded here (an earlier version of this file
# did, on the assumption it was just build-context bloat) - t/1015 clones
# "the real repository" from inside the container at runtime, which needs
# a real .git directory at the copied source path. Excluding it broke that
# test outright ("fatal: repository ... does not exist"), caught live
# during this same ticket's verify pass.
cover_db
.test-tmp
